  "extraction_notes": [
    "Forward, reverse-current, junction-capacitance, and power-derating curves were manually digitized from the supplied p. 2 figures; plotted currents in mA and nA, capacitance in pF, and power in mW were converted to SI units.",
    "Fig. 1 contains separate typical forward-characteristic curves at Ta = 25 degC and Ta = 100 degC.",
    "Fig. 2 contains separate typical reverse-characteristic curves at Ta = 25 degC and Ta = 100 degC.",
    "The forward-voltage table contains maximum values at Ta = 25 degC for IF = 1 mA, 10 mA, 50 mA, and 150 mA.",
    "The reverse-leakage table publishes maximum values of 25 nA at VR = 20 V and 1.0 uA at VR = 75 V; the single reverse_current field records the 75 V point.",
    "The reverse-breakdown voltage is specified at IR = 100 uA; the test current is recorded as a condition of breakdown voltage rather than as an independent breakdown-current specification.",
    "The power-derating curve is included as a usable plotted rating curve even though it is outside the minimum diode IV, leakage, capacitance, and recovery fitting inputs."
